{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854121-ventrue-and-nosferatu-clan-banes","id":854121,"title":"Ventrue and Nosferatu clan banes.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-27T11:41:46-07:00","id":854121,"title":"Ventrue and Nosferatu clan banes.","content":"It occured to me that part of the nosferatu clan bane fits the Ventrue much better. <br /> The bane of nosferatu is their unsettling presence and the horror they inspire in others. so why exactly is part of their clan bane that they have a harder time relating to humans? That's is how ventrue are, not nosferatu.<br /> In fact, the automatic change of presence and manip failure into dramatic failure is enough, and really the only part that is in line with the way the fluff present the nosferatu clan bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:57:38-07:00","id":854127,"title":"","content":"I think the Ventrue can get along with humans, just a specific kind of human. Nosferatu instill fear in all types of humans, generally speaking. Venture can get along with anyone whom is controlled by the allmighty dollar, which in the modern nights is many people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:15:15-07:00","id":854137,"title":"","content":"Read the descriptions again. Part of the penalty low humanity kindred experience is down to attitude, sure, but a lot of it is that they greatly resemble the walking corpses they really are. <br /> <br /> At humanity 5 a Nosferatu is taking the penalty of a humanity 3 vampire, who are described as looking &quot;deathly or sickly&quot;. At humanity 4, they're the equivalent of &quot;a moving corpse&quot;. At 3, they're taking the penalty of a statue or morbid doll. Beyond that they're at draugr levels of creep-people-the-fuck-out.<br /> <br /> Relating to people is a two-way street. It's no good understanding humans if they shit their pants at the sight of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:37:25-07:00","id":854151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854121-ventrue-and-nosferatu-clan-banes?p=854137#post854137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the descriptions again. Part of the penalty low humanity kindred experience is down to attitude, sure, but a lot of it is that they greatly resemble the walking corpses they really are.<br /> <br /> At humanity 5 a Nosferatu is taking the penalty of a humanity 3 vampire, who are described as looking &quot;deathly or sickly&quot;. At humanity 4, they're the equivalent of &quot;a moving corpse&quot;. At 3, they're taking the penalty of a statue or morbid doll. Beyond that they're at draugr levels of creep-people-the-fuck-out.<br /> <br /> Relating to people is a two-way street. It's no good understanding humans if they shit their pants at the sight of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the nosferatu clan curse is specificly mentionned as applying only to the difficulty relating to other people part of humanity and not the part about looking more and more corpse like.<br /> <br /> No I think the reason for this is much simpler than this. Someone saw humanity had social penalties and didn't realize it was actually about empathy and understanding human motivations. The language used in the clan bane description support this, it read as if they thought the social penalties were about difficulty convincing people to do things. <br /> <br /> Either they didn't realize the difference, forgot or it was changed somewhere along the line after the nosferatu curse was designed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:53:05-07:00","id":854165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854121-ventrue-and-nosferatu-clan-banes?p=854151#post854151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the nosferatu clan curse is specificly mentionned as applying only to the difficulty relating to other people part of humanity and not the part about looking more and more corpse like.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. It's specifically mentioned as applying to social penalties and not, say, sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:07:18-07:00","id":854200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854121-ventrue-and-nosferatu-clan-banes?p=854151#post854151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the nosferatu clan curse is specificly mentionned as applying only to the difficulty relating to other people part of humanity and not the part about looking more and more corpse like.<br /> <br /> No I think the reason for this is much simpler than this. Someone saw humanity had social penalties and didn't realize it was actually about empathy and understanding human motivations. The language used in the clan bane description support this, it read as if they thought the social penalties were about difficulty convincing people to do things. <br /> <br /> Either they didn't realize the difference, forgot or it was changed somewhere along the line after the nosferatu curse was designed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be a reasonable assumption to make if the books didn't go through development. But there's a whole process to avoid that kind of thing, including multiple drafts and editing passes.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's your game, do what you like, but Elfive is right about the intent of the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}